## Acceptance

In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree
to them as both strict obligations and conditions to all
your licenses.

## Copyright License

The licensor grants you a copyright license for the
software to do everything that might infringe the licensor's
copyright in the software for you to do the following,
subject to your compliance with the terms of this license:

- run the software for any permitted noncommercial purpose
- copy, modify, and share the software, including as
  incorporated into your noncommercial works, such as
  changes, fixes, and configurations

All licenses terminate automatically if you do not comply
with these terms, including the copyright license above.

## Patent License

The licensor grants you a license to any claims of patents
that the licensor can license, or becomes able to license,
that necessarily and unavoidably infringe on account of
your use of the software allowed under the copyright
license, for your use allowed under that license. You may
use that patent license only to the extent your use allowed
under that copyright license would infringe those patent
claims. That patent license terminates immediately if you
bring any patent claim against the licensor alleging that
the software infringes patent.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Any purpose is a noncommercial purpose except commerce.

Commerce is any activity or work done for the purpose of,
in furtherance of, or on behalf of any business or other
endeavor intended for commercial or monetary gain,
including internal use of the software within such an
organization.

Software development or maintenance is commerce if done
for hire, or in the course of employment, or for a
business or other endeavor intended for commercial or
monetary gain. Software support is commerce if done for
payment or other consideration.

## Notices

You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any part of
the software from you also gets a copy of these terms or
the URL for them above, as well as copies of any
plain-text lines in the software that specify limitation
of liability or prohibit modification (such as this
paragraph).

If you modify the software, you must include in any
modified copies of the software prominent notices stating
that you have modified the software.

# No Liability

***As far as the law allows, the software comes as is,
without any warranty or condition, and the licensor will
not be liable to you for any damages arising out of these
terms or the use or nature of the software, under any kind
of legal claim.***

## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these
terms, and the **software** is the software the licensor
makes available under these terms, including any portion
of it.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to
these terms.

**Your company** means any entity that employs you or that
you work for as a contractor, if the entity has contractual
responsibility for the work you do.

